# Severance Priest: "You may choose a nonland card from it." Bot1 chooses none (Choose() with an empty answer) with Mind Stone in the
# revealed hand, so nothing is exiled and Bot2's hand stays seven cards. When the Priest then dies there is no exiled card, so no one
# creates a token (the 2025-04-04 ruling).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Severance Priest
Plains x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mind Stone
Lightning Bolt
Island x4
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Severance Priest.Cast
Bot1.Choose()
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
? Exile.Count = 0
? Bot2.Revealed = Island; Island; Island; Island; Lightning Bolt; Mind Stone; Mox Ruby
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Severance Priest)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Severance Priest
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Ruby
